#WRITES
#AUTO 90
#NEEDED 0
# DE-SELECTED: question answered — the DLL locks at 200 MHz on this board
# (proven, and the HS200/HS400 probes exercise the locked DLL in practice),
# so this write-enabled characterisation is spent recon. Re-enable it on its
# own if the DLL lock ever needs re-checking (a clock or board change).
# Fast-eMMC-path reconnaissance: does the DLL lock at 200 MHz?
#
# The high-speed eMMC modes (HS200/HS400) that the fast backup
# needs run the card clock at 100-200 MHz, where the controller's
# delay-locked loop (DLL) must LOCK to the clock period instead of
# being bypassed (the bypass+start config we use at the low
# identification clock). The open hardware question is simply: does
# the DLL lock at 200 MHz on this board, and what lock value does
# it report? This probe answers that without committing any C.
#
# Register values are taken verbatim from u-boot's
# rockchip_sdhci.c rk3568 config_dll (the >= 100 MHz branch):
#   DLL reset     = DLL_CTRL bit 1
#   DLL start cfg = start-point 5 (<<16) | increment 2 (<<8) | start (bit 0)
#                 = 0x00050201
#   lock status   = DLL_STATUS0 (0x840) bit 8; lock value = bits 7:0
#
# Requires --writes (it pokes the CRU and the DLL registers, both
# inside the peripheral allowlist).
#
# Scope note: this characterises the DLL lock only. A real HS200
# bring-up additionally needs a CMD6 switch into HS200 + 8-bit bus
# and a tuning pass (CMD21) — those are SD-protocol commands the
# probe language can't issue and belong in 012-emmc.c. If the DLL
# locks here, that C work is de-risked; if it times out, HS200 on
# this board needs more investigation before we attempt it.

LOG bring the eMMC up at the low identification/transfer clock
CALL emmc_init

LOG switch CCLK_EMMC to 200 MHz (CLKSEL_CON28 sel=001)
W 0xFDD20170 0x70001000

LOG reset the DLL (DLL_CTRL bit 1), then release
W 0xFE310800 0x00000002
DELAY 4000
W 0xFE310800 0x00000000

LOG start the DLL: start-point 5, increment 2, start bit
W 0xFE310800 0x00050201

LOG poll DLL_STATUS0 bit 8 for lock (up to 100000 tries)
POLL 0xFE310840 0x00000100 0x00000100 100000

LOG read DLL_STATUS0 — bits 7:0 are the lock value if bit 8 set
R 0xFE310840

LOG read DLL_STATUS1 (per-line delay values)
R 0xFE310844

LOG DLL characterisation complete
